  "query_preview": "..Monsoon activity looks to ramp up this\nafternoon/evening, especially for locations across the Mogollon\nRim. The recent U of A WRF run shows activity initiating over the\nPeaks and White Mountains around noon today and gradually pushing\nwestward through the rest of the afternoon/evening hours. Forecast\nsoundings show plenty of instability and decent shear, so we could\nsee a handful of severe storms similar to yesterday. Not only\nthat, but localized flooding could also be a concern from training\nstorms. \n\nA more favorable monsoon pattern will set-up later this\nweekend/into next week, as the area of high pressure is projected\nto settle over the Four Corners. Prior to the incoming active\nmonsoon days, we could see a brief downward trend in convective\nactivity Friday and Saturday. The NBM still has chances for\nshowers/storms across the higher elevation locations, but we are\nnot anticipating more widespread activity until Sunday onward. \n\nOutside of precipitation, heat will continue to be a concern for a\nhandful of locations. The Extreme Heat Warning remains in place \nfor the lower elevations of the Grand Canyon and Marble/Glen \nCanyons through Friday evening, but there is potential for this to\nbe extended through the weekend. Regardless, temperatures will be\nabove normal for this time of year, so minimize outdoor activity \nduring the middle of the afternoon and stay hydrated!",
